        <p>.N ENGLISHMAN'S HOUSE IS HIS CASTLE la. or, properly speaking. ought to be. This can never be .the case, if nnkctunately a would-be householder has to resort to the Easy Payment System. a new name for the ini- .qt.itous Hire System. To furnish a house on-the Hire System. alias the Easyrrayment System, is to estaSlish and support What is. the most cruel, arbitrary extortion ever invented. The,prices charged for the goods are enormous, without any regard for quality, the agreements are one-sided, being drawn with a cuteness which would do credit to a money lender, full of despotic and arbitrary restrid)ions, suchas nut to remove the mark on the furniture, not to remove the furniture, not to wear the furniture. At all times to allow the mercenaries . to, inspect the furniture. To pay the instal- ments,regularly, and if ondsis missed to forfeit the furniture and all the moneys you may have paid, that is to say, although you might have paid £l9 on £2) worth of furniture. but missed the last payment by a •single day, the ,vultures could eanpty yourhouse and stick to the £l9 paid, as well as the furniture. Other conditions such as permissiewto break open forcibly ,night or day, the outer and inner doors of your house, in order to take away the goods, and above all.rthat no matter how 'badly and wickedly they may treat you that you undertake not to resort to legal proceedings. Be ,warned In titre, have nothing to do with easy payment or Mae system. If you require assistanze go to Mr. W. H. Worsaey, "The Pantheon, ,Gaythorne, Manchester, the largest Souse Fur- Disher in the North, who Will treat you sNittt consideration, sell you goods at the lowest cash price, and, if required, allow you time to pay for them, charging you 10 per cent over invoice pricefor the convenience. - For instance Mr. Worsley has several HOUSES OF PIM- NETURIi on 'slew at £l5 155., £2O, £25, £3O. £5O. £lOO, all at the lowest cash price, and not a penny less. Any of,the above supplied subject to credit, upon 10 per cent being added to the amount. Particulars post free.</p>
        <p>GREAT B&amp;RGAINS AT WORSLEY'S.—DRAWING- ROOM SUITE complete, solid walnut, cost £4O, price for quick sale £9 cash, tr 9 18s. credit, with Cabinet, 2 Tables. Overmantle„ Carpet, Fender, and Brasses, lc. Heavy Dining-room,Surte. emmoltte, in Mahogany, uphof- stered in Ottoman Cloth, cost £4O new, the whole lot for £ll 10s., with Side Board, Dining Table, Overmantle, and Coal Vase to match; also a Persian Carpet and Hearthrug.</p>
        <p>Magnificent Bedroom fulte : Large size Wardrobe, plate. glass. Centre door, wings for hanging, Dressing Table, Wash- stand. Threeehairs and Raft, polished satinwood, ten guineas complete with heavy brass Persian Bedstead, Curtains, Mat- tress, &amp;e., all to match. 'fen per cent added for credit. Note the following bargain .:—Complete House of Furniture' mainly second-hand, for £2O cash : £22 if by deferred pay- ments. Consists of a heavy sitting-room suite in leather, couch, two easy chairs and four single chairs, dining table. mahogany sideboard. Persian esrpet and hearthrug, brass fender, brass fire appliances, cornice and curtains, and pictures. The kitchen has a substantial dresser, chairs, arm chair, rocking chair, table, fender and fireirons, hearthrug, oilcloth. &amp;c. The bedroom is furnished with bedroom suite, chairs and rail, chamber service, brass mounted bedstead, patent wire spring mattress. Shetland wool overlay, bolster and two pillows, carpet, and fender. The stairs and the landing are fitts-d with carpets, brass rods, &amp;c. The hall or lobby is fitted with oilcloth, brass clip, three mats and a cocoa mat. The above forms the most compact, convenient lot ever offered. Other lots. £25, £3O. £36, £4O. and £5O, kqeally cheap; particulars sent on application. Every a:ticle guaranteed for five years. exchanged If not approved.</p>
