        <p>that the chariot should be sent back empty, anct that she would occupy a seat in his more easy barouche, when a loud noise was heard in the hall without, and the excited voice of Lord Trevelyaa was heard loudly demanding to be shown instantlr to the presence of his niece. (To be continued).</p>
